'' RUN: 'move( x )' (RFC 0018 V3) at every sink -- dim, assignment over a type with a written let,
'' a byval argument, 'return move( p )' of a byval parameter, a move on one return path only,
'' a self-move, an element, *p, a byref parameter -- and a type with no structors written
'' anywhere, whose string and array buffers must arrive by ADDRESS. Every case must balance and
'' each source must read back reset. The probe is tests/semantic/moves/explicit.bas; its full
'' trace is the .p2-trace there (build/movetrace.sh).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/semantic/moves/explicit.bas -o tests/codegen/moveexplicit.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/moveexplicit.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:   b=#1 t1  a=#2 t2
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: X1: ctor=2 copy=0 let=0 dtor=2 balance=ok
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:   b=#3 t3  a=#5 t5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: X2: ctor=3 copy=0 let=0 dtor=3 balance=ok
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:   (in TakeT #6 t6)
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: X3: ctor=2 copy=0 let=0 dtor=2 balance=ok
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:   b=t8  a=t8
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: X4: ctor=2 copy=1 let=0 dtor=3 balance=ok
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:   b=t11
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: X5: ctor=3 copy=0 let=0 dtor=3 balance=ok
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:   a=t14
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: X6: ctor=2 copy=0 let=0 dtor=2 balance=ok
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:   e=element  arr(1)=#18 t18
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: X7: ctor=3 copy=0 let=0 dtor=3 balance=ok
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:   dim:    same buffers: yes  list100 100  a: ubound=-1 name=""
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:   assign: same buffers: yes  b: ubound=-1 name=""
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:   (in TakeP: same buffers: yes, list100)
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:   arg:    c: ubound=-1 name=""
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:   a is usable again: reused ubound=2
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:   b=t19  a=#21 t21
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: X9: ctor=3 copy=0 let=0 dtor=3 balance=ok
